      "title": "The road to beat the heat:",
      "summary": "What if the grey roads that buckle and melt beneath record-breaking heatwaves could contribute to global cooling instead? In just the past few days the planet has offered stark reminders of the cost of inaction. In Portugal, the town of Mora sizzled at 46.6 °C on 29 June 2025, the hottest June temperature ever measured on the Iberian Peninsula.",
      "published_at": null,
